-- #1110 unit D (`Mono.TCon` carries a module identity).  The GATING SHAPE, not a
-- demonstration of the feature: two modules with NO import relationship each
-- declare a type spelled `Shape`, so after unit D the two head Monos carry
-- DIFFERENT `TyConOrigin`s while every name-equality comparison in the checker
-- still ignores the field.  The assertion is that this changes nothing.
--
-- ⚠️ Read what this pins and what it does not.  A fixture exercising the new
-- carrier would pass by construction — nothing reads the field yet, so no output
-- can depend on it.  What is worth pinning is the opposite: that a program whose
-- heads now disagree about identity behaves exactly as it did when they could not
-- disagree at all.  `shapeone` never imports `shapetwo`; its two lines of output
-- are the assertion, and the machinery that changed is in the other module.
--
-- It is also the shape the NEXT unit will move.  When a consumer starts reading
-- these origins, this is the first program whose answers could change, and a
-- diff here will name it.
--
-- Expected output, derived by hand before capture:
--   mkOne 3   = Corner 3 6   → oneSpan = 6 - 3   = 3
--   mkTwo "e" = Edge "e"     → twoLabel = "e", and `println` on a String prints
--                              it unquoted
import shapeone.{mkOne, oneSpan}
import shapetwo.{mkTwo, twoLabel}

main =
  println (oneSpan (mkOne 3))
  println (twoLabel (mkTwo "e"))
